<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54016" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταθνῄσκω</span></b> , 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατθναίσκω</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Sapph.
			62
		</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταθνάσκ-</span> codd.): fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θανοῦμαι</span>: aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέθᾰνον</span>, 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτθᾰνον</span>; late poet. aor. 1
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάθθανα</span> Maiuri<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Nuova Silloge</i><i><span class="en">
				48
			</span></i>: pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τέθνηκα</span> (v.
			infr.):—poet. Verb, <i>die away, be dying</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δὲ καταθνῄσκων προσέφη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.355
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτθανε καὶ Πάτροκλος</span>
			<i>died</i>, <i><span class="en">
				21.107
			</span></i>: in pf., <i>to be dead</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατατεθνήκασι</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζώουσι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				15.664
			</span></i>: freq. in pf.
			part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρὸς . . κατατεθνηῶτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					7.89
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				22.164
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυι κατατεθνηῶτι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.565
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκροὺς κατατεθνηῶτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.540
				</span></i>
			, etc.: used by Trag. only in sync. fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατθανοῦμαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1386
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Alc.</u>
				150
			</span></i>, etc.; and in inf. and part. of
			sync. aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατθανεῖν, κατθανών</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1290
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				873
			</span></i>, etc.: once in ind., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτθανε</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1553
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			metaph., <i>perish</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλι . . κάτθανε ἐν κηρῷ λυπεύμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					3.34
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτθανε δ᾽ ἁ μορφὰ σὺν Ἀδώνιδι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Bion
					1.31
				</span></i>
			.</div>
